(</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*end-tuple*/</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> has the same value as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\"><span class=\"kw2900\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">begin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">get</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>N<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i.<span class=\"me1\">parent_</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>bases_<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> for every integer <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">1</span> ≤ N ≤ sizeof...<span class=\"br0\">(</span>Vs<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</li></ul>\nEquivalent to: <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> i.</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/cartesian_product_view/iterator/helpers#distance_from\"><code><i>distance_from</i></code></a><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*end-tuple*/</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">6)</span> Equivalent to: <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> s<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.</div>\n<p>These functions are not visible to ordinary <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/unqualified_lookup\">unqualified</a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/qualified_lookup\">qualified lookup</a>, and can only be found by <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/adl\">argument-dependent lookup</a> when <code>cartesian_product_view::<i>iterator</i>&lt;Const&gt;</code> is an associated class of the arguments.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parame